                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                  \-module
          %p
            Similarly, compatible actions from both sides, such as for a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule"} bimodule
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bimodule+category"}> bimodule category
              \.
          %p
            Note that the term
            = succeed "," do
              %strong actegory
            %a{:href => "#McCrudden00"} McCrudden (2000)
            = succeed "," do
              %sup#fnref:1
                %a{:href => "#fn:1", :rel => "footnote"} 1
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/biactegory"} biactegory
            for the two-sided case. However, since “actegory” is a single transposition away from “category”, we prefer to use the explicit terminology on this page and elsewhere.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            For any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endofunctors"} endofunctors
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi End
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} End(A)
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal
            with respect to the (horizontal) composition (the composition of functors and the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Godement+product"} Godement product
            for natural transformations).
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mo ,
                  %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %mi l
                  %mo ,
                  %mi r
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (C,\otimes,I,l,r,a)
            a (left or right)
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              \-module category
            is a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            together with a (left or right) coherent action of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a morphism of monoidal categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi End
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to End(A)
            in the lax, colax, pseudo or strict sense (most often in pseudo-sense) or, in another terminology, a monoidal, comonoidal, strong monoidal or strict
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+functor"} monoidal functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi End
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} End(A)
            with the opposite tensor product.
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            \-module categories, colax
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "-equivariant" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-category"} strict 2-category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo
                      %mi C
                    %msup
                      %mi Act
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} _C Act^c
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monad"} monad
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo
                    %mi C
                  %msup
                    %mi Act
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} _C Act^c
            amounts to a pair of a monad in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            and a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/distributive+law"} distributive law
            between the monad and an action of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            The notion of
            = succeed "-action" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bicategories"} bicategories
            (see Baković‘s thesis).
          #ModuleCategory.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                (left)
                = succeed "-module" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is
            %ol
              %li
                a category
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒜
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              %li
                a functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊘
                      %mo :
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo ×
                      %mi 𝒜
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \oslash : \mathcal{C} \times \mathcal{A} \to \mathcal{A}
                called the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %em action
              %li
                a natural isomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi a
                      %mo →
                      %mi I
                      %mo ⊘
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_a : a \to I \oslash a
                called the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %em unitor
              %li
                a natural isomorphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi α
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                          %mo ,
                          %mi d
                          %mo ,
                          %mi a
                      %mo :
                      %mi c
                      %mo ⊘
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo ⊘
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi d
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊘
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_{c,d,a} : c \oslash (d \oslash a) \to (c \otimes d) \oslash a
                called the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %em actor
            %p
              satisfying a pentagonal and two triangular laws (see
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#KJ01"} KJ01
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi λ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
              with the unitors and associators of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %h2#connection_with_enrichment Connection with enrichment
          %p
            If a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/copowers"} copowers
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %p
            Conversely, if module category is such that the functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊘
                  %mi d
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)\oslash d:C\to D
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            for all objects
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(d,-):D\to C
            provide an enrichment of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            for which the action is a copower. See
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#KJ01"} KJ01
          %p
            More generally, supposing
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is small, the following data are equivalent: (1) a
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            in the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat C
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            (i.e. a
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+graded+category"} locally graded category
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representables"} representables
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat C
            as a monoidal category with the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
          %p
            Starting from a
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ⊘
                    %mi d
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(d,d')=hom(-\oslash d,d'):C^{op}\to Set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            for which the action is a copower. If they are not representable, it is still an enrichment, and the copowers by representables are the action.
          %p For this reason, many concepts from enriched category theory make sense for module categories too.
